Recently I got a used PC and an old (4.something) MS C compiler.
I already had 3.0j source, which I had built and modified on a
VAX.

The source says you need an least MSC 5.1 to build nethack for DOS.
I have heard that the reason it says this is that there is a bug in
5.0 that may or may not have been introduced in 5.0-- apparently
nobody on the dev team works with anything more primitive than that.

I have the original disks with C compiler, but the large model
libraries disk is has a significant manufacturing defect-- it is
an exact duplicate of the small model libraries disk.  So, for the
moment I am unable to hack nethack in the privacy of my own home.

Which brings me to a question: what is the cheapest compiler/linker
anyone has used to build 3.0j?  The full blown Microsoft C package
is expensive, and I don't know whether the QuickC subset will work.
Anybody with experience out there?

